# =============================================================================
# Streaming Shuffle Metrics -- Operator Template
# =============================================================================
#
# This file is a supplemental, classpath-resolvable metrics template for the
# Streaming Shuffle feature. It is packaged inside the spark-core JAR under
# src/main/resources and can be retrieved at runtime via:
#
#     ClassLoader.getResource(
#         "org/apache/spark/shuffle/streaming/metrics.properties.template")
#
# It is INERT by default -- every configuration entry below is commented out
# with a leading '#'. This file is not loaded by Spark's MetricsSystem
# automatically. Operators are expected to copy the desired entries into
# their active metrics configuration file (see "Usage" below).
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Relationship to conf/metrics.properties.template
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The cluster-wide metrics template shipped with Spark is
# conf/metrics.properties.template. That template is the canonical operator
# reference for enabling sinks and sources across all of Spark's components.
#
# This streaming-shuffle template is a supplemental reference focused
# exclusively on the four Dropwizard instruments exposed by the
# StreamingShuffleMetrics source (class
# org.apache.spark.shuffle.streaming.StreamingShuffleMetrics). Operators who
# already maintain a conf/metrics.properties file should append the entries
# below into that file rather than use this one directly.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Activation conditions
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Streaming shuffle metrics are emitted ONLY when the streaming shuffle manager
# is active, i.e. the SparkConf contains:
#
#     spark.shuffle.manager=streaming
#
# When Spark runs with its default sort-based shuffle manager
# (spark.shuffle.manager=sort, or the synonymous "tungsten-sort"), the
# StreamingShuffleMetrics source is NOT registered with the MetricsSystem and
# none of the shuffle.streaming.* metrics below are exposed to any sink.
# Enabling this template's source entry on an executor that is not running
# with the streaming shuffle manager is a no-op with no side effects.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Usage
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 1. Copy any desired line from the "Template entries" block below into your
#    active metrics configuration file -- typically one of:
#        conf/metrics.properties
#        $SPARK_CONF_DIR/metrics.properties
#        the file named by -Dspark.metrics.conf=<path>
# 2. Strip the leading '# ' from the copied line so the entry becomes an
#    active property.
# 3. Restart all executors. Streaming shuffle configuration is bound once
#    per executor lifetime and cannot be reconfigured dynamically in v1 --
#    configuration changes require an executor restart to take effect.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Instruments exposed by StreamingShuffleMetrics
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The StreamingShuffleMetrics source exposes the following four instruments
# under the metric name prefix "shuffle.streaming.". Each metric's JMX,
# Prometheus, Graphite, and CSV representation follows Dropwizard's standard
# naming conventions (instance + source + instrument).
#
#   1. shuffle.streaming.bufferUtilizationPercent  (Gauge[Double], 0.0 - 100.0)
#        Current buffer occupancy expressed as a percentage of the total
#        per-partition allocation. The streaming writer's per-partition
#        buffer is sized as
#            (executorMemory * spark.shuffle.streaming.bufferSizePercent)
#                / numPartitions
#        and this gauge reports the instantaneous fill level of that buffer
#        relative to its allocation. Operators use this gauge to correlate
#        spill events with actual buffer pressure.
#
#   2. shuffle.streaming.spillCount                (Counter)
#        Cumulative number of spill-to-disk events triggered by the
#        MemorySpillManager when buffer occupancy crosses the threshold
#        configured by spark.shuffle.streaming.spillThreshold (default 80).
#        A sustained non-zero rate on this counter indicates the streaming
#        shuffle is under memory pressure and is evicting buffered partitions
#        to the BlockManager's on-disk store.
#
#   3. shuffle.streaming.backpressureEvents        (Counter)
#        Cumulative number of backpressure throttle actions applied by the
#        BackpressureProtocol's token-bucket rate limiter. Each increment
#        indicates that at least one producer send was delayed because the
#        per-executor rate cap (80% of link capacity, or the explicit limit
#        from spark.shuffle.streaming.maxBandwidthMBps) was reached.
#
#   4. shuffle.streaming.partialReadInvalidations  (Counter)
#        Cumulative number of partial-read invalidations performed by the
#        StreamingShuffleReader in response to producer failure detected via
#        connection timeout (default 5 seconds). Each increment corresponds
#        to an atomic discard of all blocks previously consumed from a failed
#        producer, triggering upstream recomputation through the DAG
#        scheduler's existing fault-recovery path.
#
# =============================================================================
# Template entries
# =============================================================================
#
# The four lines below are the canonical entries for enabling the
# StreamingShuffleMetrics source and exporting it via the JMX and
# Prometheus sinks. All four lines are commented with a leading '# ' so
# this template is inert by default.

# Register the StreamingShuffleMetrics Dropwizard Source with the MetricsSystem
# on every JVM instance (driver + all executors). On executors where
# spark.shuffle.manager=streaming is active, this source publishes the four
# shuffle.streaming.* instruments described above. The wildcard '*' applies
# this binding to all instances; scope can be narrowed to "executor." if only
# executor-side emission is desired.
# *.source.shuffle.streaming.class=org.apache.spark.shuffle.streaming.StreamingShuffleMetrics

# Enable the JMX sink on every JVM instance. Exposes every registered metric
# (including the four shuffle.streaming.* instruments above) through the
# platform MBeanServer so JConsole, VisualVM, Prometheus JMX Exporter, and
# other JMX-aware monitoring integrations can scrape them.
# *.sink.jmx.class=org.apache.spark.metrics.sink.JmxSink

# Enable the Prometheus servlet sink on every JVM instance. Mounts a servlet
# that renders all registered metrics in Prometheus exposition format, making
# the four shuffle.streaming.* instruments available to a Prometheus scrape
# job targeting the driver or executor UI port.
# *.sink.prometheusServlet.class=org.apache.spark.metrics.sink.PrometheusServlet

# Configure the Prometheus servlet sink to serve the metrics document at the
# default Spark Prometheus path. Override this property to mount the servlet
# at a different path if an alternative scrape URL is required.
# *.sink.prometheusServlet.path=/metrics/prometheus
